A :CATCH that lost its `;`; the next line is the handler's first
statement. catch_clause_form reports the missing terminator with the range
on the :CATCH keyword, not on the next token (issue #255). Records
whether unexpected_token also reports the same statement.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReadSetting;
	:PARAMETERS sKey;
	:DECLARE sValue;
	:TRY;
		sValue := LSearch("SELECT SETTINGVALUE FROM SETTINGS WHERE SETTINGKEY = ?", "",, {sKey});
	:CATCH
		sValue := "";
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN sValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReadSetting;
	:PARAMETERS sKey;
	:DECLARE sValue;
	:TRY;
		sValue := LSearch("SELECT SETTINGVALUE FROM SETTINGS WHERE SETTINGKEY = ?", "",,
		                  {sKey});
	:CATCH;
		sValue := "";
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN sValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:2-6:8 error catch_clause_form: ':CATCH' is missing its ';' terminator - write ':CATCH;'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:2-6:8 error catch_clause_form: ':CATCH' is missing its ';' terminator - write ':CATCH;'
